    "type": "full-time",
    "description": "I'm rebuilding my personal brand around sharing lessons from business and OSUKA. I'm hiring a full-time Thai Business Manager to manage content and two digital product businesses: ViralHooks and Pitch Liew, my AI Skool community.\n\nHOW WE WORK: SYSTEMS + HUMAN REVIEW\nUse AI and automation with clear human approval checkpoints for ideas, accuracy, quality, and publishing.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n- Capture my notes, conversations, and lessons in an organized content bank.\n- Plan content themes, calendars, brand voice, and content guidelines.\n- Turn approved ideas into single-image posts, carousels, website articles, newsletters, podcast outlines, and long-form video scripts.\n- Edit short-form and long-form videos.\n- Plan courses: audience needs, learning outcomes, curriculum, lesson outlines, and production schedules.\n- Coordinate digital product and community operations, launches, publishing, and freelancers.\n- Build workflows, checklists, and review processes; track performance and improve execution.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- Thai candidate with strong Thai writing and communication skills; available full-time.\n- Can edit videos independently and show previous work.\n- Can plan courses and create content guidelines.\n- Organized, reliable, proactive, and able to turn rough ideas into finished work.\n- Comfortable using AI tools and carefully reviewing their output.\n- Good judgment about confidential business information.\nExperience with personal brands, courses, communities, email marketing, or digital product launches is a plus.\n\nAPPLY THROUGH FASTWORK WITH\n1. Introduction and relevant experience.\n2. Videos you have edited.\n3. A content plan, course outline, or workflow you created.\n4. Expected monthly compensation and earliest start date.\n5. How you would turn a founder's weekly lessons into content and product opportunities.\n\nCompensation and working arrangements to be discussed based on experience and fit.",
